        {
          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Now I have accurate options:\n- `--output-on-failure`: output test program output if test fails.\n- `-V` verbose, `-VV`.\n- `-O <file>, --output-log <file>`: Output to log file.\n- `--output-junit <file>`: JUnit XML.\n- `--test-output-size-passed/failed`, `--test-output-truncation`.\n- `--rerun-failed`, `--tests-from-file`.\n\nNow answer the user's question:\n\n(a) Is it worth printing the path to LastTest.log with `--output-on-failure`?\n- ctest does NOT print the log path by default, and with `--output-on-failure` you already get failing output on the console, so printing the path adds little. If anything, the useful default location is `build/debug/Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log`.\n- There's no built-in way to make ctest print \"log at: ...\". The idiomatic approach: document the location and/or use `--output-log <file>` to control it; and use `--output-junit` for machine reports.\n- Note the log path depends on the ctest invocation dir (test dir): `<test-dir>/Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log`. In their case `--test-dir build/debug` → `build/debug/Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log`.\n\n(b) How it's usually done without `--output-on-failure`:\n- ctest prints per-test progress lines (`1/233 Test #..: name .... Passed/Failed`) and at the end a summary + `The following tests FAILED:` list, but NOT the failing test's output.\n- To see details: rerun with `--output-on-failure` (or `--rerun-failed --output-on-failure`), or `-V`/`-VV` for full output, or read the log file.\n- Common workflow in CI/local: run `ctest --output-on-failure` always (cheap), or `ctest --rerun-failed --output-on-failure` for iteration.\n- Machine-readable: `--output-junit report.xml`.\n\nSo recommendation: don't add custom printing of the path into your own programs/tests; it's ctest's domain. If discoverability matters, put a line in README: \"подробный лог — build/<cfg>/Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log; быстрый повтор упавших — ctest --test-dir build/debug --rerun-failed --output-on-failure\". Optionally, define the documented test command with `--output-on-failure` so the path is rarely needed.\n\nAlso note: the `Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log` is overwritten each run, and only keeps the last run. Also `LastTestsFailed.log` list. And date-stamped dirs appear only for dashboard/`-D ExperimentalTest`.\n\nOne more nuance: `--output-log <file>` sets the log file; useful if you want a stable path. But default is fine.\n\nAlso `--test-output-size-passed`/`failed` and truncation — relevant because their output can be large.\n\nShould I suggest they could set `CTEST_OUTPUT_ON_FAILURE=1` env? That's a thing (I recall). Not in the help list, but it's an env var. Hmm, let me not assert without verification. Actually `CTEST_OUTPUT_ON_FAILURE` is a documented env variable. But not necessary.\n\nNow, plan mode: present analysis and a recommendation/plan; ask if they want a README note. No edits.\n\nLet me structure the answer:\n1. Прямой ответ: печатать путь самому не нужно; это не работа тестовых программ, а ctest. CTest этого не делает, и при `--output-on-failure` путь не нужен, т.к. вывод уже на экране.\n2. Где живёт отчёт: `build/debug/Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log` (перезаписывается каждый прогон), список упавших — `LastTestsFailed.log`. Дата-каталоги — только для dashboard.\n3. Как обычно без `--output-on-failure`: progress + summary + список FAILED, без вывода тестов. Детали — только в логе. Стандартные способы: `--output-on-failure`, `--rerun-failed --output-on-failure`, `-V`/`-VV`, открыть лог, `--output-log <file>`, `--output-junit <file>`.\n4. Рекомендация: \n   - Основная команда тестов — с `--output-on-failure` (одна команда §4.9 п.1), тогда путь к логу почти не нужен.\n   - README: указать, где лог и как повторить упавшие.\n   - Если хочется стабильный путь/машинный отчёт — `--output-log`/`--output-junit`.\n   - Не встраивать печать пути в check/run_case — не их ответственность.\n5. Offer: добавить 2-3 строки в README (когда выйдем из plan). Ask if they want it.\n\nAlso mention the nuance: printing the path unconditionally on every run is noise; and it can be wrong (depends on test-dir/cwd).\n\nLet me write concisely.\n\nOne more thing: Does ctest have a variable/way to print log location? There's `CMAKE_CTEST_ARGUMENTS`? Not relevant. There's `CTEST_...` variables. Not needed.\n\nAlso, the user might be thinking of adding it to their own test harness output (e.g., a custom target `test`). But they use ctest directly. Hmm, actually do they have a custom target `test`? The root CMakeLists has `format`, `format-check`, `enable_testing()`, tests. No `test` target explicitly (CMake auto-creates `test` target that runs ctest). So `cmake --build build/debug --target test`? That runs ctest without `--output-on-failure`. Hmm. Or they run ctest directly. In §4.9, \"make test\" equivalent. With CMake, the standard is `ctest --test-dir build`. CMake also generates a `test` target (RUN_TESTS for VS). \n\nSo maybe they want the `test` target to print the log path. Not worth it.\n\nLet me answer.\n\nI should be careful to say: with `--output-on-failure`, printing the path is redundant for failures but could help for the *other* passing tests' output, which isn't shown. Still, low value.\n\nLet me finalize.",
